    "https://www.menlo.edu/employment-opportunities/assistant-professor-of-sports-management/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Sports Management",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Sports Management - Menlo College Skip to content Athletics Parents & Families Alumni Current Students Search Visit MyMenlo About About Degrees in business and psychology are offered, with a focus on practical skills, internships, and a supportive campus community. Learn More Leadership Board of Trustees Accreditation, Rankings & Reviews Mission Statement Location Our History Maps & Directions Conference Services Summer Internship Housing Directories Campus Offices Contact Academics Academics Discover our innovative academic programs, designed to equip you with the practical skills, knowledge, and experience needed to succeed in today’s dynamic world. Learn More Undergraduate Programs Majors Minors Academic Requirements Off-Campus Study Graduate Programs Master of Arts in Sport and Performance Psychology Master of Science in Information Systems Master of Science in Financial Technology Technology Hub Institute of AI and Sustainability Bloomberg Finance Lab Academic Conferences Registrar Faculty School of Business Faculty Arts & Sciences Faculty Academic Support Services Bowman Library Course Tutoring Public Speaking Center Writing Center Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Explore admissions for Menlo College’s undergraduate and graduate programs, from requirements to financial aid. Learn More Apply Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Affordability Financial Aid & Scholarships Financial Aid Glossary Refer a Friend Tuition & Fees Explore Menlo Schedule a Visit Admissions Events Newly Admitted Students Life at Menlo Life at Menlo Experience an exciting campus life with a diverse community, engaging activities, and a supportive environment that fosters both personal and academic growth. Learn More Belonging at Menlo College Get Involved Performing Arts at Menlo College Health & Wellness Housing & Dining Residence Halls Academic Calendar Internships & Career Services Career Connect Day Student Support Student Affairs Office International Student Services Immigrant Information & Resources Veterans Support Campus Safety Transportation & Parking Campus Events Commencement OAKtoberFest TEDxMenlo College Search Visit MyMenlo GIVE APPLY Athletics Parents & Families Alumni Current Students BACK TO TOP Employment Opportunities > Assistant Professor of Sports Management Assistant Professor of Sports Management Reports to: Dean, School of Business Position Type: Full-Time, 3-year contract Compensation: $85,000-$110,000, commensurate with experience Deadline: Preference given to applications received by October 1, 2026 Target Start Date: August 1, 2027 Position Overview The School of Business at Menlo College seeks well-qualified applicants for a full-time faculty position to offer undergraduate courses in Sports Management. Courses may include introduction to sports management, research methods in sports management, sports analytics, marketing & advertising in the sports industry, sports sponsorship & sales management, ethics in sports management, history of sports, and the economics of sports, among other topics. We are particularly interested in a candidate with a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and who will contribute to diversity and equal opportunity in higher education through their teaching or other related areas. Qualifications The successful candidate should have an earned doctorate in Sports Management or in a related field from a reputable university in hand prior to the start of the Fall 2027 semester (August 2027). Preference will be given to candidates with a strong record of effective undergraduate teaching as the instructor of record. Candidates must be able and qualified to teach undergraduate Sports Management classes. They must also possess strong interpersonal skills and be able to work in a collaborative and collegial environment. Responsibilities The position requires undergraduate teaching in sports management, mentoring and advising undergraduate students, and active ongoing engagement in shared governance and other service assignments at the collegiate level, including assessment of learning. The usual faculty load is 21 units (usually seven three-unit classes) each academic year, split between the fall and spring semesters. In the first year, this load will be reduced to 18 units (six three-unit classes). About Menlo College Menlo College is doing transformative work with a significantly diverse population of students, about one-third of whom are the first in their families to attend college. Almost 100 years old, this small gem of a private college — with fewer than 900 students — is changing lives and providing a stream of inspiring, diverse and capable graduates to Silicon Valley companies and organizations. The private school offers four-year undergraduate degrees in business and psychology, and three graduate programs that leverage key areas of excellence within the College. Menlo College faculty members teach and mentor from their perspectives as scholars, entrepreneurs, managers, and community leaders. Menlo College attracts students from all over the world — young adults who are committed to learning, playing intercollegiate sports, starting and leading organizations, and volunteering in the community. The campus is located 30 miles south of San Francisco in Silicon Valley, one of the world’s most entrepreneurial and innovative locations. Silicon Valley is renowned as an innovation incubator with many opportunities for experience-based learning. Menlo College is consistently featured in lists of America’s best colleges, including citations by the Princeton Review. AffordableCollegesOnline.org (AC Online) has brought additional recognition to the quality of the Menlo College experience when the organization named Menlo as one of the 4-year colleges in California with the best lifetime return on investment (ROI). The diversity of Menlo students is reflected in its designation as a Hispanic-Serving Institution. Menlo is also one of the safest campuses anywhere; Universities.com ranks Menlo first in California, and fourth in the nation as the “safest college campus in America.” Application Process Submitted applications should include a letter of interest that discusses teaching philosophy and research interests, a current CV, names and contact information for 3 references, and teaching evaluations (if available). Submission of materials as PDF attachments is strongly encouraged. Please submit materials by October 1, 2026 to: Menlo College Attn: Human Resources Department| 1000 El Camino Real, Atherton, CA 94027-4301 Or via email to hr@menlo.edu Menlo College is an Equal Opportunity Employer with a strong commitment to diversity.  All prospective Menlo College employees are required to satisfy a background check, as well as clearance annually for the operation of a motor vehicle on behalf of Menlo College. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. All prospective Menlo College employees are required to satisfy a criminal background check. Menlo College is committed to a firm policy of equal employment opportunity. Contact Menlo 1000 El Camino Real, Atherton, CA 94027 650-543-3753 admissions@menlo.edu Menlo News Menlo College Magazine For the Media Title IX Campus Safety Employment Opportunities Privacy Policy Consumer Information Conference Services Summer Internship Housing Menlo College is committed to ensuring equal access and opportunity to all members of our campus community. We do not unlawfully discriminate in hiring, personnel practices, compensation, promotion, access to programs and activities, or educational opportunities on the basis of race, color, marital status, age, creed, national origin, sex, religion, family care status, physical or mental disability, medical condition, reproductive health decision-making, ancestry, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, citizenship status, genetic characteristic or information, or any other bases protected by state or federal laws. Inquiries regarding the College’s equal opportunity policies should be directed to the Human Resources Department via email at hr@menlo.edu. © 2025 Menlo College Secret Link"
    },
    "https://www.menlo.edu/employment-opportunities/adjunct-faculty-blockchain-cybersecurity-the-quest-for-organizational-trust/": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Blockchain, Cybersecurity & the Quest for Organizational Trust - Menlo College Skip to content Athletics Parents & Families Alumni Current Students Search Visit MyMenlo About About Degrees in business and psychology are offered, with a focus on practical skills, internships, and a supportive campus community. Learn More Leadership Board of Trustees Accreditation, Rankings & Reviews Mission Statement Location Our History Maps & Directions Conference Services Summer Internship Housing Directories Campus Offices Contact Academics Academics Discover our innovative academic programs, designed to equip you with the practical skills, knowledge, and experience needed to succeed in today’s dynamic world. Learn More Undergraduate Programs Majors Minors Academic Requirements Off-Campus Study Graduate Programs Master of Arts in Sport and Performance Psychology Master of Science in Information Systems Master of Science in Financial Technology Technology Hub Institute of AI and Sustainability Bloomberg Finance Lab Academic Conferences Registrar Faculty School of Business Faculty Arts & Sciences Faculty Academic Support Services Bowman Library Course Tutoring Public Speaking Center Writing Center Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Explore admissions for Menlo College’s undergraduate and graduate programs, from requirements to financial aid. Learn More Apply Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Affordability Financial Aid & Scholarships Financial Aid Glossary Refer a Friend Tuition & Fees Explore Menlo Schedule a Visit Admissions Events Newly Admitted Students Life at Menlo Life at Menlo Experience an exciting campus life with a diverse community, engaging activities, and a supportive environment that fosters both personal and academic growth. Learn More Belonging at Menlo College Get Involved Performing Arts at Menlo College Health & Wellness Housing & Dining Residence Halls Academic Calendar Internships & Career Services Career Connect Day Student Support Student Affairs Office International Student Services Immigrant Information & Resources Veterans Support Campus Safety Transportation & Parking Campus Events Commencement OAKtoberFest TEDxMenlo College Search Visit MyMenlo GIVE APPLY Athletics Parents & Families Alumni Current Students BACK TO TOP Employment Opportunities > Adjunct Faculty – Blockchain, Cybersecurity & the Quest for Organizational Trust Adjunct Faculty – Blockchain, Cybersecurity & the Quest for Organizational Trust Reports to: Director of Graduate Business Programs Position Type: Part-Time, Adjunct Faculty Compensation: $8,805 per course Deadline: Open until filled Target Start Date: July 2027 Position Overview Menlo College seeks well-qualified applicants for a part-time adjunct faculty position to teach Blockchain, Cybersecurity & the Quest for Organizational Trust Course in the Master of Science in Information Systems (MSIS) program. The course examines the role of blockchain, cybersecurity, and related digital technologies in establishing and maintaining trust within and between organizations. Students explore the technological, managerial, governance, and strategic dimensions of blockchain and cybersecurity an consider how organizations can manage digital risk while building trustworthy information environments. The course emphasizes the application of these technologies to contemporary organizational and business challenges rather than treating them solely as technical subjects. We are particularly interested in candidates who combine academic expertise with substantial professional experience in blockchain, cybersecurity, information security, digital trust, technology governance, or related areas. Qualifications The successful candidate should have an earned Ph.D. in Information Systems, Cybersecurity, Computer Science, Information Technology, Business, Technology Management, or a closely related field from a reputable university. Candidates must have at least three years of relevant industry experience in cybersecurity, blockchain, information security, technology risk, digital trust, or a related field. Preference will be given to candidates with demonstrated knowledge of blockchain technologies, cybersecurity principles, information security, organizational technology governance, and the business, managerial, ethical, and governance implications of emerging digital technologies, as well as prior teaching experience at the undergraduate or graduate level. Candidates must be able to integrate technical concepts with business strategy and organizational decision-making. They must also possess strong interpersonal and communication skills and be able to work in a collaborative and collegial environment. Responsibilities The position requires graduate teaching in Blockchain, Cybersecurity & the Quest for Organizational Trust, preparation and delivery of high-quality course content, and assessment of student learning. The adjunct faculty member will teach blockchain, cybersecurity, digital trust, information security, and related organizational and governance concepts; use contemporary cases and industry examples to connect theory with practice; develop assignments, projects, discussions, or other activities that encourage applied learning and critical analysis; provide timely and constructive feedback; maintain regular communication with students; support course and program assessment activities; and collaborate with the Graduate Program Director to ensure consistency with the MSIS curriculum. About Menlo College Menlo College is doing transformative work with a significantly diverse population of students, about one-third of whom are the first in their families to attend college. Almost 100 years old, this small gem of a private college – with fewer than 900 students – is changing lives and providing a stream of inspiring, diverse and capable graduates to Silicon Valley companies and organizations. The private school offers four-year undergraduate degrees in business and psychology, and three graduate programs that leverage key areas of excellence within the College. Menlo College faculty members teach and mentor from their perspectives as scholars, entrepreneurs, managers, and community leaders. Menlo College attracts students from all over the world – young adults who are committed to learning, playing intercollegiate sports, starting and leading organizations, and volunteering in the community. The campus is located 30 miles south of San Francisco in Silicon Valley, one of the world’s most entrepreneurial and innovative locations. Silicon Valley is renowned as an innovation incubator with many opportunities for experience-based learning. Menlo College is consistently featured in lists of America’s best colleges, including citations by the Princeton Review. AffordableCollegesOnline.org (AC Online) has brought additional recognition to the quality of the Menlo College experience when the organization named Menlo as one of the 4-year colleges in California with the best lifetime return on investment (ROI). The diversity of Menlo students is reflected in its designations as a Hispanic-Serving Institution. Menlo is also one of the safest campuses anywhere; Universities.com ranks Menlo first in California, and fourth in the nation as the “safest college campus in America.” Application Process Submitted applications should include a letter of interest that discusses teaching philosophy and relevant academic and professional experience, a current CV, names and contact information for 3 references, and teaching evaluations (if available). Submission of materials as PDF attachments is strongly encouraged. Please submit materials to: Menlo College Attn: Human Resources Department| 1000 El Camino Real, Atherton, CA 94027-4301 Or via email to hr@menlo.edu Menlo College is an Equal Opportunity Employer with a strong commitment to diversity.  All prospective Menlo College employees are required to satisfy a background check, as well as clearance annually for the operation of a motor vehicle on behalf of Menlo College. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. All prospective Menlo College employees are required to satisfy a criminal background check. Menlo College is committed to a firm policy of equal employment opportunity. Contact Menlo 1000 El Camino Real, Atherton, CA 94027 650-543-3753 admissions@menlo.edu Menlo News Menlo College Magazine For the Media Title IX Campus Safety Employment Opportunities Privacy Policy Consumer Information Conference Services Archive Summer Internship Housing Menlo College is committed to ensuring equal access and opportunity to all members of our campus community. We do not unlawfully discriminate in hiring, personnel practices, compensation, promotion, access to programs and activities, or educational opportunities on the basis of race, color, marital status, age, creed, national origin, sex, religion, family care status, physical or mental disability, medical condition, reproductive health decision-making, ancestry, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, citizenship status, genetic characteristic or information, or any other bases protected by state or federal laws. Inquiries regarding the College’s equal opportunity policies should be directed to the Human Resources Department via email at hr@menlo.edu. © 2025 Menlo College Secret Link"
    },
    "https://www.menlo.edu/employment-opportunities/adjunct-faculty-data-repositories-and-cloud-infrastructure/": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Data Repositories and Cloud Infrastructure - Menlo College Skip to content Athletics Parents & Families Alumni Current Students Search Visit MyMenlo About About Degrees in business and psychology are offered, with a focus on practical skills, internships, and a supportive campus community. Learn More Leadership Board of Trustees Accreditation, Rankings & Reviews Mission Statement Location Our History Maps & Directions Conference Services Summer Internship Housing Directories Campus Offices Contact Academics Academics Discover our innovative academic programs, designed to equip you with the practical skills, knowledge, and experience needed to succeed in today’s dynamic world. Learn More Undergraduate Programs Majors Minors Academic Requirements Off-Campus Study Graduate Programs Master of Arts in Sport and Performance Psychology Master of Science in Information Systems Master of Science in Financial Technology Technology Hub Institute of AI and Sustainability Bloomberg Finance Lab Academic Conferences Registrar Faculty School of Business Faculty Arts & Sciences Faculty Academic Support Services Bowman Library Course Tutoring Public Speaking Center Writing Center Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Explore admissions for Menlo College’s undergraduate and graduate programs, from requirements to financial aid. Learn More Apply Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Affordability Financial Aid & Scholarships Financial Aid Glossary Refer a Friend Tuition & Fees Explore Menlo Schedule a Visit Admissions Events Newly Admitted Students Life at Menlo Life at Menlo Experience an exciting campus life with a diverse community, engaging activities, and a supportive environment that fosters both personal and academic growth. Learn More Belonging at Menlo College Get Involved Performing Arts at Menlo College Health & Wellness Housing & Dining Residence Halls Academic Calendar Internships & Career Services Career Connect Day Student Support Student Affairs Office International Student Services Immigrant Information & Resources Veterans Support Campus Safety Transportation & Parking Campus Events Commencement OAKtoberFest TEDxMenlo College Search Visit MyMenlo GIVE APPLY Athletics Parents & Families Alumni Current Students BACK TO TOP Employment Opportunities > Adjunct Faculty – Data Repositories and Cloud Infrastructure Adjunct Faculty – Data Repositories and Cloud Infrastructure Reports to: Director of Graduate Business Programs Position Type: Part-Time, Adjunct Faculty Compensation: $8,805 per course Deadline: Open until filled Target Start Date: June 2027 Position Overview Menlo College seeks well-qualified applicants for a part-time adjunct faculty position to teach Data Repositories and Cloud Infrastructure Course in the Master of Science in Information Systems (MSIS) program, Analytics Track. Cloud technologies serve as the collection of services and solutions many organizations develop on, deploy on, rely upon, and conduct critical business on for their day-to-day operations. Many organizations have migrated from traditional data repositories and data systems to cloud data lakes and platforms appropriate for reporting, aggregating, analyzing, and making decisions based on resulting conclusions. The course presents cloud service and deployment models as well as the services, solutions, infrastructure, platforms, and software tools used to accommodate sizeable data repositories. We are particularly interested in a candidate who combines academic expertise with handson professional experience in cloud computing, data infrastructure, and enterprise information systems. Qualifications The successful candidate should have an earned Ph.D. in Information Systems, Computer Science, Data Science, Information Technology, Computer Engineering, or a closely related field from a reputable university. Candidates must have at least three years of relevant industry experience in cloud computing, data engineering, data architecture, database systems, or related areas. Preference will be given to candidates with demonstrated knowledge of cloud infrastructure, data repositories, data lakes, database technologies, modern data architectures, and major cloud environments, as well as prior teaching experience at the undergraduate or graduate level. Candidates must be able to connect technical concepts with business and organizational applications. They must also possess strong interpersonal skills and be able to work in a collaborative and collegial environment. Responsibilities The position requires graduate teaching in Data Repositories and Cloud Infrastructure, preparation and delivery of lectures, demonstrations, exercises, and applied learning activities, and assessment of student learning. The adjunct faculty member will teach concepts related to cloud service and deployment models, data storage, data repositories, data lakes, infrastructure, platforms, and associated software tools; incorporate contemporary industry technologies and business use cases; develop practical assignments or projects; provide timely feedback; maintain regular communication with students; support course and program learning-outcome assessment; and collaborate with the Graduate Program Director as needed to maintain alignment with the MSIS curriculum. About Menlo College Menlo College is doing transformative work with a significantly diverse population of students, about one-third of whom are the first in their families to attend college. Almost 100 years old, this small gem of a private college – with fewer than 900 students – is changing lives and providing a stream of inspiring, diverse and capable graduates to Silicon Valley companies and organizations. The private school offers four-year undergraduate degrees in business and psychology, and three graduate programs that leverage key areas of excellence within the College. Menlo College faculty members teach and mentor from their perspectives as scholars, entrepreneurs, managers, and community leaders. Menlo College attracts students from all over the world – young adults who are committed to learning, playing intercollegiate sports, starting and leading organizations, and volunteering in the community. The campus is located 30 miles south of San Francisco in Silicon Valley, one of the world’s most entrepreneurial and innovative locations. Silicon Valley is renowned as an innovation incubator with many opportunities for experience-based learning. Menlo College is consistently featured in lists of America’s best colleges, including citations by the Princeton Review. AffordableCollegesOnline.org (AC Online) has brought additional recognition to the quality of the Menlo College experience when the organization named Menlo as one of the 4-year colleges in California with the best lifetime return on investment (ROI). The diversity of Menlo students is reflected in its designations as a Hispanic-Serving Institution. Menlo is also one of the safest campuses anywhere; Universities.com ranks Menlo first in California, and fourth in the nation as the “safest college campus in America.” Application Process Submitted applications should include a letter of interest that discusses teaching philosophy and relevant academic and professional experience, a current CV, names and contact information for 3 references, and teaching evaluations (if available). Submission of materials as PDF attachments is strongly encouraged. Please submit materials to: Menlo College Attn: Human Resources Department| 1000 El Camino Real, Atherton, CA 94027-4301 Or via email to hr@menlo.edu Menlo College is an Equal Opportunity Employer with a strong commitment to diversity.  All prospective Menlo College employees are required to satisfy a background check, as well as clearance annually for the operation of a motor vehicle on behalf of Menlo College. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. All prospective Menlo College employees are required to satisfy a criminal background check. Menlo College is committed to a firm policy of equal employment opportunity. Contact Menlo 1000 El Camino Real, Atherton, CA 94027 650-543-3753 admissions@menlo.edu Menlo News Menlo College Magazine For the Media Title IX Campus Safety Employment Opportunities Privacy Policy Consumer Information Conference Services Archive Summer Internship Housing Menlo College is committed to ensuring equal access and opportunity to all members of our campus community. We do not unlawfully discriminate in hiring, personnel practices, compensation, promotion, access to programs and activities, or educational opportunities on the basis of race, color, marital status, age, creed, national origin, sex, religion, family care status, physical or mental disability, medical condition, reproductive health decision-making, ancestry, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, citizenship status, genetic characteristic or information, or any other bases protected by state or federal laws. Inquiries regarding the College’s equal opportunity policies should be directed to the Human Resources Department via email at hr@menlo.edu. © 2025 Menlo College Secret Link"
    },
    "https://www.menlo.edu/employment-opportunities/adjunct-faculty-leadership-in-the-fourth-industrial-revolution/": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Leadership in the Fourth Industrial Revolution - Menlo College Skip to content Athletics Parents & Families Alumni Current Students Search Visit MyMenlo About About Degrees in business and psychology are offered, with a focus on practical skills, internships, and a supportive campus community. Learn More Leadership Board of Trustees Accreditation, Rankings & Reviews Mission Statement Location Our History Maps & Directions Conference Services Summer Internship Housing Directories Campus Offices Contact Academics Academics Discover our innovative academic programs, designed to equip you with the practical skills, knowledge, and experience needed to succeed in today’s dynamic world. Learn More Undergraduate Programs Majors Minors Academic Requirements Off-Campus Study Graduate Programs Master of Arts in Sport and Performance Psychology Master of Science in Information Systems Master of Science in Financial Technology Technology Hub Institute of AI and Sustainability Bloomberg Finance Lab Academic Conferences Registrar Faculty School of Business Faculty Arts & Sciences Faculty Academic Support Services Bowman Library Course Tutoring Public Speaking Center Writing Center Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Explore admissions for Menlo College’s undergraduate and graduate programs, from requirements to financial aid. Learn More Apply Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Affordability Financial Aid & Scholarships Financial Aid Glossary Refer a Friend Tuition & Fees Explore Menlo Schedule a Visit Admissions Events Newly Admitted Students Life at Menlo Life at Menlo Experience an exciting campus life with a diverse community, engaging activities, and a supportive environment that fosters both personal and academic growth. Learn More Belonging at Menlo College Get Involved Performing Arts at Menlo College Health & Wellness Housing & Dining Residence Halls Academic Calendar Internships & Career Services Career Connect Day Student Support Student Affairs Office International Student Services Immigrant Information & Resources Veterans Support Campus Safety Transportation & Parking Campus Events Commencement OAKtoberFest TEDxMenlo College Search Visit MyMenlo GIVE APPLY Athletics Parents & Families Alumni Current Students BACK TO TOP Employment Opportunities > Adjunct Faculty – Leadership in the Fourth Industrial Revolution Adjunct Faculty – Leadership in the Fourth Industrial Revolution Reports to: Director of Graduate Business Programs Position Type: Part-Time, Adjunct Faculty Compensation: $8,805 per course Deadline: Open until filled Target Start Date: January & February 2027 Position Overview Menlo College seeks well-qualified applicants for a part-time adjunct faculty position to teach Leadership in the Fourth Industrial Revolution Course in the Master of Science in Information Systems (MSIS) program, Analytics Track. The course examines how emerging and disruptive technologies are transforming organizations, industries, leadership practices, and the nature of work. Topics include artificial intelligence, automation, digital transformation, technological disruption, organizational change, innovation, and the economic and societal implications of the Fourth Industrial Revolution. We are particularly interested in a candidate who can combine strong academic preparation with substantial industry experience and help graduate students connect leadership concepts and emerging technologies to contemporary organizational challenges. Qualifications The successful candidate should have an earned Ph.D. in Information Systems, Business, Management, Organizational Leadership, Technology Management, Innovation, or a closely related field from a reputable university. Candidates must have at least three years of relevant industry or professional experience. Preference will be given to candidates with demonstrated knowledge of digital transformation, emerging technologies, organizational change, innovation, or technology leadership, as well as prior teaching experience at the undergraduate or graduate level. Candidates must be able to integrate academic concepts with current industry practices and real-world applications. They must also possess strong interpersonal and communication skills and be able to work in a collaborative and collegial environment. Responsibilities The position requires graduate teaching in Leadership in the Fourth Industrial Revolution, preparation and delivery of high-quality course content, and assessment of student learning. The adjunct faculty member will develop course materials consistent with the approved course description and learning outcomes; incorporate current business cases, emerging technologies, and industry examples; assess student learning through appropriate assignments, projects, presentations, or examinations; provide timely and constructive feedback; maintain appropriate communication with students and program leadership; and participate in course and program assessment activities as requested. About Menlo College Menlo College is doing transformative work with a significantly diverse population of students, about one-third of whom are the first in their families to attend college. Almost 100 years old, this small gem of a private college – with fewer than 900 students – is changing lives and providing a stream of inspiring, diverse and capable graduates to Silicon Valley companies and organizations. The private school offers four-year undergraduate degrees in business and psychology, and three graduate programs that leverage key areas of excellence within the College. Menlo College faculty members teach and mentor from their perspectives as scholars, entrepreneurs, managers, and community leaders. Menlo College attracts students from all over the world – young adults who are committed to learning, playing intercollegiate sports, starting and leading organizations, and volunteering in the community. The campus is located 30 miles south of San Francisco in Silicon Valley, one of the world’s most entrepreneurial and innovative locations. Silicon Valley is renowned as an innovation incubator with many opportunities for experience-based learning. Menlo College is consistently featured in lists of America’s best colleges, including citations by the Princeton Review. AffordableCollegesOnline.org (AC Online) has brought additional recognition to the quality of the Menlo College experience when the organization named Menlo as one of the 4-year colleges in California with the best lifetime return on investment (ROI). The diversity of Menlo students is reflected in its designations as a Hispanic-Serving Institution. Menlo is also one of the safest campuses anywhere; Universities.com ranks Menlo first in California, and fourth in the nation as the “safest college campus in America.” Application Process Submitted applications should include a letter of interest that discusses teaching philosophy and relevant academic and professional experience, a current CV, names and contact information for 3 references, and teaching evaluations (if available). Submission of materials as PDF attachments is strongly encouraged. Please submit materials to: Menlo College Attn: Human Resources Department| 1000 El Camino Real, Atherton, CA 94027-4301 Or via email to hr@menlo.edu Menlo College is an Equal Opportunity Employer with a strong commitment to diversity.  All prospective Menlo College employees are required to satisfy a background check, as well as clearance annually for the operation of a motor vehicle on behalf of Menlo College. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. All prospective Menlo College employees are required to satisfy a criminal background check. Menlo College is committed to a firm policy of equal employment opportunity. Contact Menlo 1000 El Camino Real, Atherton, CA 94027 650-543-3753 admissions@menlo.edu Menlo News Menlo College Magazine For the Media Title IX Campus Safety Employment Opportunities Privacy Policy Consumer Information Conference Services Archive Summer Internship Housing Menlo College is committed to ensuring equal access and opportunity to all members of our campus community. We do not unlawfully discriminate in hiring, personnel practices, compensation, promotion, access to programs and activities, or educational opportunities on the basis of race, color, marital status, age, creed, national origin, sex, religion, family care status, physical or mental disability, medical condition, reproductive health decision-making, ancestry, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, citizenship status, genetic characteristic or information, or any other bases protected by state or federal laws. Inquiries regarding the College’s equal opportunity policies should be directed to the Human Resources Department via email at hr@menlo.edu. © 2025 Menlo College Secret Link"
    },
    "https://www.menlo.edu/employment-opportunities/career-development-librarian/": {
      "title": "Career Development Librarian",
      "description": "Career Development Librarian - Menlo College Skip to content Athletics Parents & Families Alumni Current Students Search Visit MyMenlo About About Degrees in business and psychology are offered, with a focus on practical skills, internships, and a supportive campus community. Learn More Leadership Board of Trustees Accreditation, Rankings & Reviews Mission Statement Location Our History Maps & Directions Conference Services Summer Internship Housing Directories Campus Offices Contact Academics Academics Discover our innovative academic programs, designed to equip you with the practical skills, knowledge, and experience needed to succeed in today’s dynamic world. Learn More Undergraduate Programs Majors Minors Academic Requirements Off-Campus Study Graduate Programs Master of Arts in Sport and Performance Psychology Master of Science in Information Systems Master of Science in Financial Technology Technology Hub Institute of AI and Sustainability Bloomberg Finance Lab Academic Conferences Registrar Faculty School of Business Faculty Arts & Sciences Faculty Academic Support Services Bowman Library Course Tutoring Public Speaking Center Writing Center Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Explore admissions for Menlo College’s undergraduate and graduate programs, from requirements to financial aid. Learn More Apply Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Affordability Financial Aid & Scholarships Financial Aid Glossary Refer a Friend Tuition & Fees Explore Menlo Schedule a Visit Admissions Events Newly Admitted Students Life at Menlo Life at Menlo Experience an exciting campus life with a diverse community, engaging activities, and a supportive environment that fosters both personal and academic growth. Learn More Belonging at Menlo College Get Involved Performing Arts at Menlo College Health & Wellness Housing & Dining Residence Halls Academic Calendar Internships & Career Services Career Connect Day Student Support Student Affairs Office International Student Services Immigrant Information & Resources Veterans Support Campus Safety Transportation & Parking Campus Events Commencement OAKtoberFest TEDxMenlo College Search Visit MyMenlo GIVE APPLY Athletics Parents & Families Alumni Current Students BACK TO TOP Employment Opportunities > Career Development Librarian Career Development Librarian Reports to: Director of Library Services Position Type: Full-time, 12 months, Exempt, Primarily On-Site Compensation: $90,000 Position Overview The Career Development Librarian works collaboratively across departments to provide students with foundational skills for academic success, student retention, and career success. These efforts include the development of digital learning objects, workshops, and individual appointments with students. The position will also select books and other materials in support of student skills and career development. The Career Development Librarian will help shape the direction of this position and ensure a foundation is laid for long-term continued work in these areas. The Career Development Librarian is funded by a 5-year Strengthening Institutions Program (SIP) grant facilitated by The Employment and Training Administration at the U.S. Department of Labor. The position is currently funded for 1 year, and subsequent employment is dependent on continued federal funding for the remaining 4 years of the grant. Responsibilities Designs and delivers special workshops for all Menlo College students and student workers to strengthen foundational skills including:* Information literacy: Concepts represented in the ACRL Framework AI literacy: Ability to use and evaluate AI tools, and to think critically about their output Digital literacy: Basic skills such as online privacy, file types, keyboard shortcuts, cloud vs. local storage, formatting documents, etc. Critical thinking skills: Problem solving and independent thinking Financial literacy: Basic skills such as how to budget, do taxes, etc. Career exploration: Finding resources to evaluate companies, assess job markets, and research possible career paths *Some workshops may be created in collaboration with other departments, guest speakers, or other collaborators, as well as drawn from reputable online teaching resources. Candidate is not expected to be an expert in all areas listed. Supports student research skills and other skills listed above through a variety of formats, including: 1:1 appointments (both remote and in person) Front desk help at the library Research help through Chat, email, phone, and other channels Works closely with the Student Success Librarian to support and expand the library’s Information Literacy Program, which may include providing course-integrated instruction sessions Collaborates with Internships and Career Services, Academic Support, Academic Affairs, faculty members, and other departments across campus to ensure synergy and high quality student support Creates engaging digital learning objects and other content for the library website Creates templates, lesson plans, and other documentation to promote long-term sustainability of created content Selects library books and other materials to support essential skill and knowledge development for academic and career success Assesses student outcomes and library services as related to efforts funded by the SIP grant Stays up to date with relevant trends in higher education, library and information science, and the job market for graduating students Other duties as assigned Work Schedule Typical work schedule may be either Monday through Friday or Sunday through Thursday, depending on candidate’s availability Occasional evening and weekend hours may be required Qualifications Master’s degree in Library and Information Science from a program accredited by the American Library Association Teaching experience required, including the ability to apply the Association of College and Research Libraries’ Framework for Information Literacy in instructional design Experience developing digital learning objects, such as videos, learning modules, surveys, and research guides An understanding of foundational AI principles and skills and the ability to engage in continuous learning to support the evolving needs of students. Reference experience and ability to use, select, and assess resources in the social sciences and business Experience with and continuing interest in library and instructional technologies (e.g., Springshare LibApps, WMS Library Management System, Canvas LMS) and use of digital media in education (e.g. screencasting, social media, user experience design) Strong customer service skills, and experience working with diverse populations Knowledge or experience in supporting student career development, retention, and success Knowledge of general principles of library organization and management About Bowman Library Bowman Library provides collections and services to inspire, engage, and advance teaching, learning, and research at Menlo College. Currently, instructional support includes course-integrated research sessions, individual consultations, and an asynchronous information literacy module required of all undergraduate students. Located in the heart of the campus, the library is beloved by students and faculty and fosters a positive learning environment. A learning commons, reservable study rooms, comfortable seating areas, study carrels, and student-run late night hours all contribute to a sense of community and place for students throughout their Menlo College experience. About Menlo College Located in the heart of Silicon Valley, Menlo College is a small, residential liberal arts and business college dedicated to preparing students to be Future Ready Now. Through a highly personalized educational experience that combines rigorous academics, applied learning, mentorship, and direct access to one of the world’s most innovative economies, Menlo College helps students convert education into measurable career and life outcomes. Guided by advisors invested in every student’s journey, Menlo empowers graduates to explore, adapt, lead with purpose, and launch lives of impact in a rapidly changing world. Application Process Interested individuals should submit a cover letter and current resume/CV. Submission of all application materials in an electronic format is highly encouraged. Please email materials to: Menlo College Attn: Human Resources Department| 1000 El Camino Real, Atherton, CA 94027-4301 Or via email to hr@menlo.edu Menlo College is an Equal Opportunity Employer with a strong commitment to diversity.  All prospective Menlo College employees are required to satisfy a background check, as well as clearance annually for the operation of a motor vehicle on behalf of Menlo College Applicants should be authorized to work in the United States without visa sponsorship. Contact Menlo 1000 El Camino Real, Atherton, CA 94027 650-543-3753 admissions@menlo.edu Menlo News Menlo College Magazine For the Media Title IX Campus Safety Employment Opportunities Privacy Policy Consumer Information Conference Services Archive Summer Internship Housing Menlo College is committed to ensuring equal access and opportunity to all members of our campus community. We do not unlawfully discriminate in hiring, personnel practices, compensation, promotion, access to programs and activities, or educational opportunities on the basis of race, color, marital status, age, creed, national origin, sex, religion, family care status, physical or mental disability, medical condition, reproductive health decision-making, ancestry, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, citizenship status, genetic characteristic or information, or any other bases protected by state or federal laws. Inquiries regarding the College’s equal opportunity policies should be directed to the Human Resources Department via email at hr@menlo.edu. © 2025 Menlo College Secret Link"
    },
    "https://www.menlo.edu/employment-opportunities/admissions-counselor": {
      "title": "Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Admissions Counselor - Menlo College Skip to content Athletics Parents & Families Alumni Current Students Search Visit MyMenlo About About Degrees in business and psychology are offered, with a focus on practical skills, internships, and a supportive campus community. Learn More Leadership Board of Trustees Accreditation, Rankings & Reviews Mission Statement Location Our History Maps & Directions Conference Services Summer Internship Housing Directories Campus Offices Contact Academics Academics Discover our innovative academic programs, designed to equip you with the practical skills, knowledge, and experience needed to succeed in today’s dynamic world. Learn More Undergraduate Programs Majors Minors Academic Requirements Off-Campus Study Graduate Programs Master of Arts in Sport and Performance Psychology Master of Science in Information Systems Master of Science in Financial Technology Technology Hub Institute of AI and Sustainability Bloomberg Finance Lab Academic Conferences Registrar Faculty School of Business Faculty Arts & Sciences Faculty Academic Support Services Bowman Library Course Tutoring Public Speaking Center Writing Center Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Explore admissions for Menlo College’s undergraduate and graduate programs, from requirements to financial aid. Learn More Apply Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Affordability Financial Aid & Scholarships Financial Aid Glossary Refer a Friend Tuition & Fees Explore Menlo Schedule a Visit Admissions Events Newly Admitted Students Life at Menlo Life at Menlo Experience an exciting campus life with a diverse community, engaging activities, and a supportive environment that fosters both personal and academic growth. Learn More Belonging at Menlo College Get Involved Performing Arts at Menlo College Health & Wellness Housing & Dining Residence Halls Academic Calendar Internships & Career Services Career Connect Day Student Support Student Affairs Office International Student Services Immigrant Information & Resources Veterans Support Campus Safety Transportation & Parking Campus Events Commencement OAKtoberFest TEDxMenlo College Search Visit MyMenlo GIVE APPLY Athletics Parents & Families Alumni Current Students BACK TO TOP Admissions Counselor Title: Admissions Counselor Reports to: Director of Admissions Position Type: Full-time, 12-month, exempt position with benefits Salary: $68,640 DOE Location: Atherton, CA – in-person position with travel involved Position Overview: As a vital member of our admissions team, the Admissions Counselor plays a pivotal role in attracting students to Menlo College, where our mission is to “ignite potential and educate students to make meaningful contributions in the innovation economy.” This position involves developing and implementing effective and personalized recruitment strategies, overseeing communications for a specific geographic territory, evaluating applications, and building strong relationships with high schools. The Admissions Counselor guides prospective students through the application process, champions Menlo College’s values, and ensures a positive experience for prospective students and their families. This role directly contributes to the College’s enrollment goals. Key Responsibilities: Represent the College at various events, including college fairs, high school presentations, on-campus events, and other programming. Select, schedule, and coordinate visits to high schools and college fairs in assigned geographic areas to achieve recruitment goals for Menlo College. Maintain up-to-date knowledge of target high schools and college fairs in assigned geographic areas and develop strategies for effective territory management. Cultivate effective relationships with high school personnel, alumni, and influencers who impact prospective students’ college decisions. Build and maintain relationships with Menlo staff and faculty who can support recruiting efforts. Facilitate connections between prospective students and their families and appropriate stakeholders within Menlo for a personalized experience. Provide guidance to prospective students and their families on the admissions process, financial aid, academic programs, and student life at Menlo College. Collect and review application materials for admissions decisions to be made, adhering to Menlo’s admissions policies and best practices. Develop and execute targeted strategies to enhance conversion rates of prospective students within the admissions funnel for assigned geographic regions. Ensure accurate recording and updating of information in the admissions database (Salesforce) by maintaining up-to-date records of prospective student interactions, application statuses, and other relevant data. Collaborate with the Executive Director of Marketing and Communications to manage strategic communications with high school and independent counselors through various channels. Efficiently handle a high volume of communication across diverse channels, including phone & video calls, text messages, emails, and hand-written notes, while maintaining a professional and organized approach in a fast-paced environment. Meet weekly outreach targets to prospective students. Assist in developing and delivering on and off-campus events and programs for prospective students, families, and counselors. Contribute to the smooth functioning of the admissions office by providing tours and supporting the operations team as needed. Contribute to the yearly planning and evaluation of recruitment and admission programs. Respond promptly to new inquiries and follow up on communications in a timely manner with all constituents, including prospective students, families, and other stakeholders. Be proactive in addressing questions and concerns that may arise throughout the admissions process, and guide students and their families through each step of the process with care, attention to detail, and a friendly and professional demeanor. Participate in ongoing professional development and stay updated on Menlo’s academic programs, extracurricular opportunities, and student support services to accurately represent the college. Perform other duties as assigned, contributing to the overall success of the admissions team and Menlo College Qualifications: Education and Experience: Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field. 1-2 years of college admissions or sales experience for the Admissions Counselor role, with demonstrated leadership skills and success in achieving or exceeding enrollment goals. Skills and Abilities: Strong cross-cultural, interpersonal, and writing skills. Exceptional customer service skills with the ability to communicate effectively across diverse populations. Proficiency in MS Office Suite, Google Workspace, and presentation platforms. Knowledge of Salesforce is a plus. Ability to work in a fast-paced environment with accuracy. Familiarity with federal and state financial aid programs. Collaborative team player with a strong commitment to achieving admissions team goals, while also capable of working independently to meet performance targets. Ability to maintain a high level of discretion and confidentiality. Familiarity with FERPA regulations. Ability to lift packages of 35-40 lbs. Spanish language proficiency is a plus. Availability and Travel: Typical office hours are 9 AM – 6 PM, Monday to Friday, with periodic weekends and evenings dedicated to various tasks, including but not limited to: admissions events, outreach events, and call campaigns. The role involves extensive travel, including visits to high schools, community colleges, and college fairs. Must possess a valid driver’s license. About Menlo College Located in the heart of Silicon Valley, Menlo College is a small, residential liberal arts and business college dedicated to preparing students to be Future Ready Now. Through a highly personalized educational experience that combines rigorous academics, applied learning, mentorship, and direct access to one of the world’s most innovative economies, Menlo College helps students convert education into measurable career and life outcomes. Guided by advisors invested in every student’s journey, Menlo empowers graduates to explore, adapt, lead with purpose, and launch lives of impact in a rapidly changing world. Application Process Interested individuals should submit a cover letter and current resume/CV. Submission of all application materials in an electronic format is highly encouraged. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis beginning December 8,2025. Please email materials to: hr@menlo.edu Menlo College Attn: Director of Human Resources 1000 El Camino Real, Atherton, CA 94027-4301 Menlo College is an Equal Opportunity Employer with a strong commitment to diversity. All prospective Menlo College employees are required to satisfy a background check, as well as clearance annually for the operation of a motor vehicle on behalf of Menlo College. Applicants should be authorized to work in the U.S. without sponsorship. Contact Menlo 1000 El Camino Real, Atherton, CA 94027 650-543-3753 admissions@menlo.edu Menlo News Menlo College Magazine For the Media Title IX Campus Safety Employment Opportunities Privacy Policy Consumer Information Conference Services Archive Summer Internship Housing Menlo College is committed to ensuring equal access and opportunity to all members of our campus community. We do not unlawfully discriminate in hiring, personnel practices, compensation, promotion, access to programs and activities, or educational opportunities on the basis of race, color, marital status, age, creed, national origin, sex, religion, family care status, physical or mental disability, medical condition, reproductive health decision-making, ancestry, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, citizenship status, genetic characteristic or information, or any other bases protected by state or federal laws. Inquiries regarding the College’s equal opportunity policies should be directed to the Human Resources Department via email at hr@menlo.edu. © 2025 Menlo College Secret Link"
    },
    "https://www.menlo.edu/employment-opportunities/assistant-director-of-admissions/": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Admissions",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Admissions - Menlo College Skip to content Athletics Parents & Families Alumni Current Students Search Visit MyMenlo About About Degrees in business and psychology are offered, with a focus on practical skills, internships, and a supportive campus community. Learn More Leadership Board of Trustees Accreditation, Rankings & Reviews Mission Statement Location Our History Maps & Directions Conference Services Summer Internship Housing Directories Campus Offices Contact Academics Academics Discover our innovative academic programs, designed to equip you with the practical skills, knowledge, and experience needed to succeed in today’s dynamic world. Learn More Undergraduate Programs Majors Minors Academic Requirements Off-Campus Study Graduate Programs Master of Arts in Sport and Performance Psychology Master of Science in Information Systems Master of Science in Financial Technology Technology Hub Institute of AI and Sustainability Bloomberg Finance Lab Academic Conferences Registrar Faculty School of Business Faculty Arts & Sciences Faculty Academic Support Services Bowman Library Course Tutoring Public Speaking Center Writing Center Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Explore admissions for Menlo College’s undergraduate and graduate programs, from requirements to financial aid. Learn More Apply Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Affordability Financial Aid & Scholarships Financial Aid Glossary Refer a Friend Tuition & Fees Explore Menlo Schedule a Visit Admissions Events Newly Admitted Students Life at Menlo Life at Menlo Experience an exciting campus life with a diverse community, engaging activities, and a supportive environment that fosters both personal and academic growth. Learn More Belonging at Menlo College Get Involved Performing Arts at Menlo College Health & Wellness Housing & Dining Residence Halls Academic Calendar Internships & Career Services Career Connect Day Student Support Student Affairs Office International Student Services Immigrant Information & Resources Veterans Support Campus Safety Transportation & Parking Campus Events Commencement OAKtoberFest TEDxMenlo College Search Visit MyMenlo GIVE APPLY Athletics Parents & Families Alumni Current Students BACK TO TOP Assistant Director of Admissions Title: Assistant Director of Admissions Reports to: Director of Admissions Position Type: Full-time, 12-month, exempt position with benefits Salary: $72,000-$76,000 Location: Atherton, CA – in-person position with travel involved Position Overview: The Assistant Director of Admissions supports the development and execution of Menlo College’s undergraduate recruitment strategy by managing assigned territories, representing the College at recruitment events, building relationships with high school counselors, community colleges, and community organizations, and providing personalized guidance to prospective students and families throughout the admissions process. The Assistant Director develops and maintains recruitment partnerships, contributes to communication and yield efforts, participates in application review, supports on- and off-campus events, collaborates with campus partners to ensure consistent messaging, and maintains accurate records in the CRM to support data-informed decision-making and overall enrollment goals. Key Responsibilities: Territory Management & Recruitment (45%) Develop and implement a strategic, data-informed recruitment plan for assigned territories. Represent Menlo College at high school visits, college fairs, community college events, and virtual programs. Build and maintain relationships with high school counselors, community college personnel, and community organizations. Provide timely, personalized outreach to prospective students and families through phone, email, text, and in-person meetings. Assist with on-campus recruitment events, including campus tours, info sessions, visit programs, and admitted student events. Maintain a high level of customer service throughout the admissions process. Application Review & Yield (25%) Review and evaluate undergraduate applications using holistic review practices. Participate in committee discussions and make recommendations for admission. Support yield and conversion initiatives, including personalized outreach to admitted students and families. Collaborate with Financial Aid, Student Affairs, Student Success, and Academic Affairs to support yield and onboarding initiatives. Partnership Development & Communication (20%) Cultivate and sustain partnerships with high schools, community colleges, community-based organizations, and nonprofits. Serve as the primary liaison for educational partners, coordinating communication, programming, and engagement activities. Support the implementation of communication plans developed by the Director of Admissions and Marketing & Communications. Assist with targeted outreach campaigns to students, families, and counselors. Provide feedback to leadership on messaging gaps and opportunities. Engage with prospective students using CRM-driven outreach and nurture campaigns. Data, Reporting & Operations (10%) Maintain accurate student interaction records and status updates in Salesforce. Use data to monitor territory performance and adjust strategies accordingly. Assist with routine administrative tasks to support smooth admissions operations. Support front desk operations when needed to ensure a welcoming visitor experience. Other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field. Strong interpersonal, presentation, and public speaking skills for student-facing outreach. Excellent written and verbal communication skills with a high level of customer service orientation. Ability to build positive relationships with diverse students, families, counselors, and community partners. Ability to represent Menlo College and clearly communicate the value proposition of the Menlo experience. Strong organizational and time management skills with attention to detail. Ability to interpret and clearly explain admissions requirements, academic programs, scholarships, and financial aid basics. Comfortable with high-volume outreach including calling, texting, and email communication. Ability to handle confidential information with professionalism and discretion. Strong problem-solving skills and ability to adapt in a fast-paced, deadline-driven environment. Ability to work independently and collaboratively as part of a team. Proficiency with Google Workspace, Microsoft Office, and basic data tools. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in a relevant field. Experience using CRM systems (Salesforce, Slate, TargetX, Element451, or similar). Experience planning or supporting recruitment events and campus programs. Familiarity with using funnel data, reports, or territory analytics to inform outreach. Experience working with diverse, first-generation, transfer, or underrepresented student populations. Knowledge of regional and national admissions organizations (e.g., NACAC, WACAC, College Board). Experience in higher education, student services, college advising, or related fields. About Menlo College Located in the heart of Silicon Valley, Menlo College is a small, residential liberal arts and business college dedicated to preparing students to be Future Ready Now. Through a highly personalized educational experience that combines rigorous academics, applied learning, mentorship, and direct access to one of the world’s most innovative economies, Menlo College helps students convert education into measurable career and life outcomes. Guided by advisors invested in every student’s journey, Menlo empowers graduates to explore, adapt, lead with purpose, and launch lives of impact in a rapidly changing world. Application Process Interested individuals should submit a cover letter and current resume. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis beginning December 8, 2025. Please email materials to: hr@menlo.edu Menlo College Attn: Director of Human Resources 1000 El Camino Real, Atherton, CA 94027-4301 Menlo College is an Equal Opportunity Employer with a strong commitment to diversity. All prospective Menlo College employees are required to satisfy a background check, as well as clearance annually for the operation of a motor vehicle on behalf of Menlo College. Applicants should be authorized to work in the U.S. without sponsorship. Contact Menlo 1000 El Camino Real, Atherton, CA 94027 650-543-3753 admissions@menlo.edu Menlo News Menlo College Magazine For the Media Title IX Campus Safety Employment Opportunities Privacy Policy Consumer Information Conference Services Archive Summer Internship Housing Menlo College is committed to ensuring equal access and opportunity to all members of our campus community. We do not unlawfully discriminate in hiring, personnel practices, compensation, promotion, access to programs and activities, or educational opportunities on the basis of race, color, marital status, age, creed, national origin, sex, religion, family care status, physical or mental disability, medical condition, reproductive health decision-making, ancestry, military or veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, citizenship status, genetic characteristic or information, or any other bases protected by state or federal laws. Inquiries regarding the College’s equal opportunity policies should be directed to the Human Resources Department via email at hr@menlo.edu. © 2025 Menlo College Secret Link"
